yaml/number/binary
description: Integer in base two - 0b and the bits
- >
  An integer in base two - `0b` followed by binary digits. A YAML 1.1 notation: the 1.2 core
  schema reads it as an ordinary string; the spelling is reserved, opt-in vocabulary,
  classified the moment a reader decodes it:
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  a: 0b101010
